{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `bucket_of` in `repo/histogram.py`. A value exactly on the top edge (`value == width * n_buckets`) now goes into the last bucket, index `n_buckets - 1`. Both visible tests pass.\n\n```python\n    if value == width * n_buckets:\n        return n_buckets - 1\n    return value // width\n```\n\nI also removed the `# BUG` comment.\n\nI made the clamp apply only to the exact top edge, as you described. A value above the top edge still returns an index past the end and will still error. That keeps bad input visible instead of quietly counting it in the last bucket. If you want every value above the range to land in the last bucket too, change it to `min(value // width, n_buckets - 1)`.\n\n`old_bucket` calls `bucket_of`, so it gets the fix as well."}]},"session_id":"4c800b4a-a47f-4593-b57e-da43d3d27d55"}
